Krita Nova 06 - screen tracker: no SAFE ASSERT when rotating with the brush editor open

KisScreenMigrationTracker (used by the brush editor's scratchpad) keeps its screen
signal connections when the native window it tracks is destroyed (KisPopupButtonFrame
recreates its window). Rotating on Android then reports a DPI change with no window and
hit KIS_SAFE_ASSERT(!trackedWidget()->isVisible()) in KisScreenMigrationTracker.cpp.
Reattach to the widget's current native window instead (or drop the stale connections).

diff --git a/libs/widgetutils/KisScreenMigrationTracker.cpp b/libs/widgetutils/KisScreenMigrationTracker.cpp
index dfaa123..f5854c8 100644
--- a/libs/widgetutils/KisScreenMigrationTracker.cpp
+++ b/libs/widgetutils/KisScreenMigrationTracker.cpp
@@ -92,9 +92,22 @@ void KisScreenMigrationTracker::slotScreenLogicalResolutionChanged(qreal value)
 void KisScreenMigrationTracker::slotResolutionCompressorTriggered()
 {
     if (!m_connectedTopLevelWindow) {
-        // the tracker is not yet initialized, it should happen only
-        // when the widget have not yet been shown at least once
-        KIS_SAFE_ASSERT_RECOVER_NOOP(!trackedWidget()->isVisible());
+        // Either the tracker is not initialized yet (the widget has never been
+        // shown), or the native window we were connected to has been destroyed
+        // in the meantime, e.g. KisPopupButtonFrame recreates its window when
+        // (de)tached, while the screen signals stayed connected. On Android a
+        // rotation then reports a DPI change with no window to attach it to.
+        //
+        // Krita Nova: instead of asserting, reattach to the widget's current
+        // native window if it has one (this emits the screen signals), and
+        // otherwise drop the stale screen connections.
+        QWidget *widget = trackedWidget();
+        QWindow *window = widget && widget->window() ? widget->window()->windowHandle() : nullptr;
+        if (window) {
+            connectToNativeWindow(window);
+        } else {
+            m_screenConnections.clear();
+        }
         return;
     }
     Q_EMIT sigScreenOrResolutionChanged(m_connectedTopLevelWindow->screen());
